As of Oct 12, the record for Alleghany County runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids. October to November came in under 90% of normal in 37 of those years, more than any other pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 169% of normal in January to February and only 65% in March to April. Grid 21200 had its driest year in 1963 at 69%.</p>"}
